 "note": "Two columns joined on each line, separated by reading order. Left column: PRIMARY SCHOOL STAFF (line 1: Chivilo ... Hathaway) -> primary; then ELEMENTARY AND PRIMARY SCHOOL AIDES (heading line 17: Baker x4 ... Steele x2) -> per the printed parenthetical, (Elementary) -> passios (bare 'Elementary' = Passios, inferred) and (Primary) -> primary. Right column: HEALTH SERVICES (heading line 1: Asher, Heimberg, Neuschatz, Hobbs, Richards, Brown) and CUSTODIAL STAFF (heading line 22: Okerman, then custodians). Page school district-wide because it is three groups. Mrs. Carol A. Baker (lines 18, 20, 22, 24) and Joan E. Damon (32, 34) and Rachel M. Steele (56, 59) are printed once per duty, so one entry per printed line (4, 2 and 2 entries for the same person: Baker's four are Math Aide (Elementary), Playground Aide (Primary), Cafeteria Aide (Primary), Clerical Aide (Primary)). Physicians (Asher, Heimberg 'Football Doctor', Neuschatz) -> district-wide; nurses by printed parenthetical (Elementary -> passios, Middle -> middle, High -> high). Custodians by printed building, Okerman 'Supervisor/Foreman of Bldgs. & Grounds' -> district-wide. Paul G. Doyle is 'High School (Day Shift)' with a note he transferred to Elementary School 11/17/80 (he is also on p121 under Elementary): school high as printed on this line. Resignation notes inline. Line 63 page number. Honorifics: this page prints Dr. and 'R. N.' only. Integration pass, 31 Oct 2026: school bus contractors, drivers and volunteers moved from entries to ignored (not school staff; every 1971-1980 page treated alike), and `middle` written `turkey-hill` -- the 1972 and 1974 listings print the building as `Turkey Hill Middle School (Grades 5-7)`, the town's one middle school."
